<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Join</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>join</a>   (at a guild master)
</pre>
<p>Type join at a guild master to become a member of that guild. You can belong to 
more than one guild (see <a cmd='#'>Help Guilds</a>), but your profession, not the guild, 
decides what training costs you (see <a cmd='#'>Help Professions</a>).
</p><p>A guild master may first want something of you: many guilds have a quest you 
must finish before they take you in, and the guild master tells you about it 
when you type join. Some guilds won't take members of certain other guilds, 
and a guild that has banished you won't take you back.
</p><p>To leave a guild, insult its guild master (see <a cmd='#'>Help Insult</a>).
</p><p>To join a group of players, see <a cmd='#'>Help Groups</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Guilds</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Professions</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Insult</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Groups</a>
</pre>




</div>